# ---------------- Ray tracing (GI) ----------------
option.RT_LIGHTS=Ray Traced Block Lights
option.RT_LIGHTS.comment=Sends a shadow ray from every pixel straight to a nearby light source instead of hoping a random ray hits it. This is what makes a torch cast a real shadow, light leak through the holes of a trapdoor and colored lights actually fill a room. §eThe single most important setting for lighting mood
option.RT_LIGHT_STRENGTH=Block Light Strength (RT)
option.RT_LIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of the ray traced block lights. Raise it if torches and colored lights feel too weak to create a mood
option.RT_LIGHT_SAMPLES=Light Candidates
option.RT_LIGHT_SAMPLES.comment=How many light sources are considered each frame before one is picked for the shadow ray. Higher reacts faster and is less noisy in rooms with many lights, but costs performance
option.RT_LIGHT_SIZE=Light Size
option.RT_LIGHT_SIZE.comment=Multiplier on the real size of a light source. The softness of a shadow comes from how big the light is, and the size is taken from the shape measured during voxelization: a torch is a thin post and keeps its sharp shadow, while a glowstone block is a full cube and casts a soft one, so neighbouring blocks merge into a single even shadow. 1.0 is the physically correct size. 0 turns every light into a point, which gives hard edges but makes each block cast its own separate shadow
option.RT_LIGHT_RANGE=Light Range
option.RT_LIGHT_RANGE.comment=How far a block light can reach. Lights further away than this are ignored, which keeps performance in builds with many torches
option.RT_LIGHT_FALLOFF=Light Falloff
option.RT_LIGHT_FALLOFF.comment=How quickly block light fades with distance. Lower spreads light further and fills rooms more, higher gives tighter pools of light
option.GI_ENABLED=Ray Traced GI
option.GI_ENABLED.comment=Traces one light ray per pixel through a voxel copy of the world. Gives colored light from torches and lava, light bouncing off walls and real ambient occlusion. §cThe most expensive feature of the pack
option.VOXEL_RANGE=Voxel Range
option.VOXEL_RANGE.comment=Width of the ray traced area around you. Outside of it the vanilla light map is used. Bigger uses more video memory and makes rays slower
value.VOXEL_RANGE.128=128 blocks
value.VOXEL_RANGE.192=192 blocks
value.VOXEL_RANGE.256=256 blocks
option.GI_MAX_STEPS=GI Ray Steps
option.GI_MAX_STEPS.comment=How many block boundaries a GI ray may cross before it gives up. Higher lets light travel further through caves and rooms. §eMain GI performance setting
option.GI_MAX_DISTANCE=GI Ray Distance
option.GI_MAX_DISTANCE.comment=Maximum length of a GI ray. A ray that reaches it without hitting anything counts as seeing the sky
suffix.GI_MAX_DISTANCE=\ blocks
option.GI_STRENGTH=GI Strength
option.GI_STRENGTH.comment=Multiplier for all indirect light. 0 turns indirect light off completely, which is useful to look at direct light alone
option.EMISSION_STRENGTH=Light Source Strength
option.EMISSION_STRENGTH.comment=Overall brightness of light emitting blocks, both in ray tracing and on their own surfaces. Colors per block type are on the Emissive Block Colors page
option.GI_BOUNCES=Light Bounces
option.GI_BOUNCES.comment=How many times a light ray bounces before it stops. One bounce only carries light from surfaces the ray hits directly. Two or more let color travel: sunlight hitting an orange ceiling then spreading orange light through the room. §eThe main setting for colour bleeding, and the most expensive one
option.GI_SATURATION=Colour Bleeding
option.GI_SATURATION.comment=Boosts the colour of indirect light. Higher values make a red wall throw clearly red light onto its surroundings instead of a barely visible tint
option.GI_SKY_STRENGTH=Sky Light in GI
option.GI_SKY_STRENGTH.comment=How much light a GI ray receives when it escapes to the sky. Lower makes shaded areas darker and more contrasted
option.GI_SUN_BOUNCE=Sunlight Bounce
option.GI_SUN_BOUNCE.comment=Brightness of sunlight that bounces off lit surfaces into shaded areas. Makes rooms with sunny windows glow
option.GI_HIT_AMBIENT=Multi Bounce Ambient
option.GI_HIT_AMBIENT.comment=Extra ambient light added where rays hit, to imitate more than one bounce. Higher makes shaded areas softer and brighter
option.GI_FIREFLY_CLAMP=Firefly Clamp
option.GI_FIREFLY_CLAMP.comment=Limits how bright a single ray sample can be. Lower removes sparkling white dots near light sources but makes small lights dimmer
option.VOXEL_SHAPES=Block Shapes
option.VOXEL_SHAPES.comment=Measures the real shape of every block so torches, doors, trapdoors, slabs and anvils no longer block a whole cube of light. Shadows and reflections follow the actual shape, for example light passing through the gaps of a trapdoor. Turning this off makes those blocks stop casting ray traced shadows entirely
option.VOXELIZE_TRANSLUCENT_EMITTERS=Translucent Light Sources
option.VOXELIZE_TRANSLUCENT_EMITTERS.comment=Light sources drawn in the translucent layer, such as the nether portal, also emit ray traced light in their own color
option.EMISSION_SHAPE_BOOST=Small Light Compensation
option.EMISSION_SHAPE_BOOST.comment=A torch is much smaller than a block, so rays hit it less often and it would look dim. This brightens small light sources to compensate. 0 disables it, which is physically honest but makes torches darker
option.EMISSION_SHAPE_BOOST_MAX=Compensation Limit
option.EMISSION_SHAPE_BOOST_MAX.comment=Upper limit of the compensation. Lower it if very small light sources look too bright
option.CUTOUT_SHADOW_MASK=Shaped Holes in Shadows
option.CUTOUT_SHADOW_MASK.comment=The holes in blocks like trapdoors and doors are in the texture, not in the shape, so a voxel grid normally turns them into an evenly translucent plate. This records where the holes are inside each block and lets block light through exactly there, so a torch behind a trapdoor casts the hole pattern on the floor. Costs some video memory
option.CUTOUT_MASK_RES=Hole Detail
option.CUTOUT_MASK_RES.comment=Resolution of the hole grid stored inside each block. 16 matches the Minecraft texture exactly and catches single pixel holes. 8 uses a quarter of the video memory but merges small holes together, which makes the cast shadow wrong
option.VOXELIZE_LEAVES=Leaves Block Light
option.VOXELIZE_LEAVES.comment=Leaves are added to the voxel world so forests shade the ground below. Turn it off for brighter forests
option.AUTO_EMITTERS=Auto Detect Light Sources
option.AUTO_EMITTERS.comment=Blocks that emit light but are not listed in block.properties, such as modded lamps, also cast ray traced light using their texture color. Needs the Iris block emission feature

# ---------------- Denoiser ----------------
option.GI_TEMPORAL_FRAMES=Accumulation Frames
option.GI_TEMPORAL_FRAMES.comment=How many past frames are averaged with the current noisy GI. More frames means less noise but lighting reacts slower when a torch is placed or removed
suffix.GI_TEMPORAL_FRAMES=\ frames
option.GI_TEMPORAL_DEPTH_TOLERANCE=History Rejection Tolerance
option.GI_TEMPORAL_DEPTH_TOLERANCE.comment=How much the depth may differ before old frames are thrown away. Too low causes noise while moving, too high leaves ghost trails behind objects
option.GI_DENOISE=Spatial Denoiser
option.GI_DENOISE.comment=Blurs GI with neighbouring pixels on the same surface while keeping edges sharp
option.GI_DENOISE_SAMPLES=Denoiser Samples
option.GI_DENOISE_SAMPLES.comment=How many neighbouring pixels are blended together. Raise it when the image still looks grainy after increasing accumulation frames. Above 12 the sample disc is reused with a rotation, so the cost keeps rising linearly
option.GI_DENOISE_RADIUS=Blur Radius (fresh)
option.GI_DENOISE_RADIUS.comment=Blur radius right after the history was reset, for example when something moved. Larger hides noise better but smears lighting
suffix.GI_DENOISE_RADIUS=\ px
option.GI_DENOISE_MIN_RADIUS=Blur Radius (settled)
option.GI_DENOISE_MIN_RADIUS.comment=Blur radius once the history is fully accumulated. 0 shows only the temporal result
suffix.GI_DENOISE_MIN_RADIUS=\ px
option.GI_DENOISE_NORMAL_WEIGHT=Edge Sharpness
option.GI_DENOISE_NORMAL_WEIGHT.comment=How strictly pixels facing different directions are kept apart. Higher keeps corners crisp but leaves more noise

