option.EMIT_MINERAL_BLOCKS=Mineral Blocks Glow
option.EMIT_MINERAL_BLOCKS.comment=Redstone, lapis, emerald, diamond, amethyst and coal blocks become light sources in their own color. When off they behave as polished blocks
option.EMIT_TINTED_I=Own Color Power
option.EMIT_TINTED_I.comment=Brightness of blocks that emit light in their own texture color, such as the 16 candle colors. A blue candle gives blue light without needing a separate setting for every color
option.EMIT_TINTED_SAT=Own Color Saturation
option.EMIT_TINTED_SAT.comment=How saturated the light taken from the texture is. 0 makes it white, higher values make the color more intense

# ---------------- Reflections ----------------
option.RT_REFLECTIONS=Ray Traced Reflections
option.RT_REFLECTIONS.comment=Reflections are found by tracing rays through the voxel world, so they also show things that are off screen. When off, only the sky is reflected
option.REFLECTION_SCREEN_LOOKUP=Textured Reflections
option.REFLECTION_SCREEN_LOOKUP.comment=If the reflected point is visible on screen, its real textured and lit pixel is used instead of the flat voxel color
option.REFLECTION_STEPS=Reflection Ray Steps
option.REFLECTION_STEPS.comment=How many blocks a reflection ray may cross. Higher also reflects far away terrain
option.REFLECTION_MAX_DISTANCE=Reflection Distance
option.REFLECTION_MAX_DISTANCE.comment=Maximum length of a reflection ray
suffix.REFLECTION_MAX_DISTANCE=\ blocks
option.SSR_FALLBACK=Screen Space Fallback
option.SSR_FALLBACK.comment=When the voxel ray misses, the screen image is searched instead. Reflects mobs, players, plants and terrain outside the voxel range
option.SSR_MAX_STEPS=Screen Space Steps
option.SSR_MAX_STEPS.comment=Maximum steps of the screen space search. Higher is more accurate but slower
option.SSR_THICKNESS=Screen Space Thickness
option.SSR_THICKNESS.comment=How thick objects are assumed to be. Too low misses thin objects, too high creates wrong reflections behind objects
suffix.SSR_THICKNESS=\ blocks
option.WATER_REFLECTIONS=Water Reflections
option.WATER_REFLECTIONS.comment=Reflections on water surfaces
option.GLASS_REFLECTIONS=Glass Reflections
option.GLASS_REFLECTIONS.comment=Reflections on stained glass, ice and other translucent blocks
option.GLASS_REFLECTION_STRENGTH=Glass Reflection Strength
option.GLASS_REFLECTION_STRENGTH.comment=How strong reflections on glass are
option.GLASS_REFRACTION=Glass Refraction
option.GLASS_REFRACTION.comment=Light bends as it passes through glass and ice, so what is behind them shifts slightly
option.GLASS_REFRACTION_STRENGTH=Glass Refraction Strength
option.GLASS_REFRACTION_STRENGTH.comment=How much the view behind glass is shifted
option.GLASS_REFRACTION_DEPTH=Glass Thickness
option.GLASS_REFRACTION_DEPTH.comment=How thick glass is assumed to be when bending light. Using the real distance to the wall behind the glass turned it into a magnifying lens, so this is kept small. Raise it only if you want a stronger lens effect
option.REFLECTION_BLOCK_LIGHT=Block Light in Reflections
option.REFLECTION_BLOCK_LIGHT.comment=Surfaces seen in a reflection also receive light from torches and other block lights. Without it, reflections indoors go black because there is no sunlight to light them, which makes metal blocks and doors look like black holes. Costs one extra ray on reflective pixels
option.BLOCK_REFLECTIONS=Block Reflections
option.BLOCK_REFLECTIONS.comment=Reflections on polished and metal blocks listed in block.properties and on surfaces from LabPBR resource packs
option.POLISHED_SMOOTHNESS=Polished Block Smoothness
option.POLISHED_SMOOTHNESS.comment=Smoothness of polished stones, quartz, concrete and glazed terracotta. 1 is a perfect mirror
option.METAL_SMOOTHNESS=Metal Block Smoothness
option.METAL_SMOOTHNESS.comment=Smoothness of iron, gold, copper and netherite blocks. 1 is a perfect mirror
option.REFLECTION_MIN_SMOOTHNESS=Minimum Smoothness
option.REFLECTION_MIN_SMOOTHNESS.comment=Surfaces rougher than this get no ray traced reflections. Lower adds reflections to more surfaces and costs performance
option.ROUGH_REFLECTION_JITTER=Rough Reflection Spread
option.ROUGH_REFLECTION_JITTER.comment=How much reflections on less smooth surfaces are scattered. 0 makes every reflection a sharp mirror
option.SUN_SPECULAR=Sun Highlights
option.SUN_SPECULAR.comment=Bright highlight of the sun on smooth surfaces
option.LABPBR=LabPBR Materials
option.LABPBR.comment=Reads smoothness and metalness from LabPBR resource packs. Without such a resource pack this does nothing
option.LABPBR_EMISSION=LabPBR Emission
option.LABPBR_EMISSION.comment=Reads glowing parts of textures from LabPBR resource packs

# ---------------- Coloured light ----------------
screen.TRANSMISSION=Coloured Light
screen.TRANSMISSION.comment=How light behaves when it passes through stained glass, ice and blocks with holes in them
option.COLORED_SHADOWS=Coloured Sun Shadows
option.COLORED_SHADOWS.comment=Sunlight passing through stained glass takes its colour, so a red window throws a red patch on the floor. Water tints sunlight blue in the same way
option.GLASS_TRANSMISSION=Coloured Block Light
option.GLASS_TRANSMISSION.comment=Torches and other block lights are also tinted when their light passes through stained glass. Without this only sunlight is coloured
option.GLASS_TINT_STRENGTH=Glass Tint Strength
option.GLASS_TINT_STRENGTH.comment=How strongly glass colours the light passing through it. 0 lets light through unchanged
option.TRANSMISSION_FROM_ALPHA=Light Through Holes
option.TRANSMISSION_FROM_ALPHA.comment=Blocks whose texture has holes, such as trapdoors and iron bars, let part of the light through instead of blocking it like a solid box. §eNote: the amount of light is taken from the texture, so the shadow softens rather than taking the exact shape of the holes
option.SHADOW_TINT_BRIGHTNESS=Coloured Shadow Brightness
option.SHADOW_TINT_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Brightness of the light that comes through coloured glass

# ---------------- Lighting ----------------
option.SUN_BRIGHTNESS=Sun Brightness
option.SUN_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Brightness of direct sunlight and the sun disc
option.MOON_BRIGHTNESS=Moon Brightness
option.MOON_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Brightness of moonlight at night. 0 makes nights completely dark away from light sources
option.SKY_BRIGHTNESS=Sky Brightness
option.SKY_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Brightness of the sky color and the ambient light that comes from it
option.MIN_LIGHT=Minimum Light
option.MIN_LIGHT.comment=Light added everywhere so that dark caves are not pitch black
option.BLOCKLIGHT_STRENGTH=Block Light Strength
option.BLOCKLIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of the vanilla light map glow around torches and other lights. This light has no shadows. Ray traced light is added separately
option.BLOCKLIGHT_CURVE=Block Light Falloff
option.BLOCKLIGHT_CURVE.comment=How fast vanilla block light fades with distance. Higher gives smaller, more focused pools of light
option.LIGHTMAP_RT_BLEND=Light Map in RT Area
option.LIGHTMAP_RT_BLEND.comment=How much vanilla block light remains inside the ray traced area. 0 uses only ray traced light, which is more realistic but darker and noisier. 1 keeps vanilla block light fully
option.BLOCKLIGHT_R=Red
option.BLOCKLIGHT_R.comment=Red part of the vanilla block light color
option.BLOCKLIGHT_G=Green
option.BLOCKLIGHT_G.comment=Green part of the vanilla block light color
option.BLOCKLIGHT_B=Blue
option.BLOCKLIGHT_B.comment=Blue part of the vanilla block light color
option.HAND_LIGHT=Held Light
option.HAND_LIGHT.comment=Holding a torch or another light source lights up your surroundings
option.HAND_LIGHT_STRENGTH=Held Light Strength
option.HAND_LIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of the held light
option.HAND_LIGHT_RANGE=Held Light Range
option.HAND_LIGHT_RANGE.comment=How far the held light reaches
option.FOLIAGE_TRANSLUCENCY=Foliage Translucency
option.FOLIAGE_TRANSLUCENCY.comment=Sunlight shines through leaves and plants
option.LEAK_FIX=Light Leak Fix
option.LEAK_FIX.comment=Uses the vanilla sky light map to stop sky light and sunlight from leaking into caves and closed rooms. Turn it off only for testing
option.NETHER_AMBIENT=Nether Ambient Light
option.NETHER_AMBIENT.comment=Brightness of the reddish ambient light in the Nether
option.END_AMBIENT=End Ambient Light
option.END_AMBIENT.comment=Brightness of the purple ambient light in the End

# ---------------- Shadows ----------------
option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow Resolution
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=Resolution of the shadow map. Higher gives sharper shadow edges and costs video memory and performance
option.shadowDistance=Shadow Distance
option.shadowDistance.comment=How far from you shadows are drawn. A larger area spreads the same resolution thinner, so shadows get blurrier
suffix.shadowDistance=\ blocks
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS=Shadow Softness
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS.comment=Blur of shadow edges. 0 gives hard pixel edges
option.SHADOW_SAMPLES=Shadow Samples
option.SHADOW_SAMPLES.comment=Number of samples used for soft shadows. Lower is faster but grainier
option.SHADOW_DISTORTION=Shadow Distortion
option.SHADOW_DISTORTION.comment=Gives more shadow resolution close to you and less far away. 0 spreads resolution evenly
option.SHADOW_BIAS=Shadow Bias
option.SHADOW_BIAS.comment=Pushes shadow tests away from surfaces. Raise it if you see striped shadow acne, lower it if shadows detach from objects
option.sunPathRotation=Sun Angle
option.sunPathRotation.comment=Tilts the path of the sun so shadows fall at an angle even at noon
