option.DITHERING=Dithering
option.DITHERING.comment=Adds invisible noise that removes color banding in smooth gradients like the sky

# ---------------- Debug ----------------
option.DEBUG_VIEW=View
option.DEBUG_VIEW.comment=Shows the selected internal data instead of the final image. Hover the ? rows below for full descriptions. 1 Albedo: unlit surface color. 2 Normals: surface direction. 3 Light map: red block light, blue sky light. 4 Material ID. 5 Smoothness and metal. 6 Emission category. 7 Depth. 8 GI raw single ray. 9 GI accumulated. 10 GI denoised. 11 GI history length. 12 Direct sunlight. 13 Shadow. 14 Block light. 15 Voxel world. 16 Voxel types. 17 Voxel range. 18 Reflections only. 19 Translucent surfaces. 20 Emission. 21 Voxel shapes. 22 Ray traced block lights
value.DEBUG_VIEW.0=§7Off
value.DEBUG_VIEW.1=1 Albedo
value.DEBUG_VIEW.2=2 Normals
value.DEBUG_VIEW.3=3 Light map
value.DEBUG_VIEW.4=4 Material ID
value.DEBUG_VIEW.5=5 Smoothness / metal
value.DEBUG_VIEW.6=6 Emission category
value.DEBUG_VIEW.7=7 Depth
value.DEBUG_VIEW.8=8 GI raw (1 ray)
value.DEBUG_VIEW.9=9 GI accumulated
value.DEBUG_VIEW.10=10 GI denoised
value.DEBUG_VIEW.11=11 GI history length
value.DEBUG_VIEW.12=12 Direct light
value.DEBUG_VIEW.13=13 Shadow
value.DEBUG_VIEW.14=14 Block light
value.DEBUG_VIEW.15=15 Voxel world
value.DEBUG_VIEW.16=16 Voxel types
value.DEBUG_VIEW.17=17 Voxel range
value.DEBUG_VIEW.18=18 Reflections
value.DEBUG_VIEW.19=19 Translucent surfaces
value.DEBUG_VIEW.20=20 Emission
value.DEBUG_VIEW.21=21 Voxel shapes
value.DEBUG_VIEW.22=22 Block lights (RT)
option.DEBUG_SPLIT=Split Screen
option.DEBUG_SPLIT.comment=The left half shows the debug view and the right half shows the normal image. Handy for comparing a buffer with the final result
option.DEBUG_NAN_CHECK=Highlight Broken Pixels
option.DEBUG_NAN_CHECK.comment=Pixels that contain NaN or infinite values turn magenta. Such values usually come from dividing by zero or from pow with a negative base. Once they reach the GI history they spread, so they are worth hunting down
option.DEBUG_SHADOW_OVERLAY=Shadow Map Preview
option.DEBUG_SHADOW_OVERLAY.comment=Shows the shadow map in the bottom left corner. Dark is close to the sun, bright is far away. Useful to check shadow distance and distortion
option.DEBUG_FREEZE_NOISE=Freeze Noise
option.DEBUG_FREEZE_NOISE.comment=Uses the same random ray directions every frame, so the GI noise pattern stops changing and settings can be compared without flicker. Leave it off for normal play because it makes GI biased
option.DEBUG_HELP_GBUFFER=§7? G-buffer views (1-7)
option.DEBUG_HELP_GBUFFER.comment=These views show what opaque geometry wrote into the G-buffer. §e1 Albedo§r: unlit texture color. Black or magenta areas mean the texture could not be read. §e2 Normals§r: surface direction. Red is east, green is up, blue is south. If the color changes across one flat surface, the normal is wrong. §e3 Light map§r: red block light, blue sky light. Deep caves should be black. §e4 Material§r: gray solid, light green plant, dark green leaves, yellow light source, pink hand, black unlit. A block with the wrong color is in the wrong group of block.properties. §e5 Smoothness§r: red smoothness, green F0, blue metal. §e6 Emission category§r: light emitting surfaces in their category color, white shades are LabPBR emission strength. §e7 Depth§r: near is dark, far is bright, sky is dark blue
option.DEBUG_HELP_GI=§7? GI views (8-11)
option.DEBUG_HELP_GI.comment=The stages of ray traced indirect light. §e8 GI raw§r: the result of one ray per pixel this frame, heavy noise is normal. If it is completely black the voxel grid may be empty, check view 15. §e9 GI accumulated§r: average over frames. If it leaves trails while moving, lower History Rejection Tolerance. §e10 GI denoised§r: the final indirect light used for lighting. §e11 GI history§r: red means just reset, green means fully accumulated. If the screen stays red while the camera is still, temporal accumulation is broken
option.DEBUG_HELP_LIGHT=§7? Lighting views (12-14, 20)
option.DEBUG_HELP_LIGHT.comment=The light components that build the final color. They are added together and multiplied by albedo. §e12 Direct light§r: sunlight or moonlight including highlights. §e13 Shadow§r: white is lit, black is shadowed. If you see striped patterns, raise Shadow Bias. §e14 Block light§r: vanilla light map and held light. §e20 Emission§r: the own glow of surfaces, for example torch flames and lava
option.DEBUG_HELP_VOXEL=§7? Voxel views (15-17)
option.DEBUG_HELP_VOXEL.comment=The voxel world that the ray tracer sees, traced directly from the camera. §e15 Voxel world§r: the average texture color of each block. If a block is missing here it was not voxelized. §e16 Voxel types§r: gray solid, green leaves, cyan polished, gold metal, listed light sources in their own color, pink auto detected lights. §e17 Voxel range§r: green is ray traced, yellow is the transition, red is outside where the vanilla light map is used. §e21 Voxel shapes§r: gray is a full cube, yellow to red are increasingly small shapes such as torches and carpets. Use it to check whether a block was measured correctly
option.DEBUG_HELP_TOOLS=§7? Other views (18-19) and tools
option.DEBUG_HELP_TOOLS.comment=§e18 Reflections§r: only the light that reflections add to the scene. §e22 Block lights§r: only the ray traced light from torches, lava and other light sources, without sunlight. Use it to check whether a light source is in the list and whether its shadows are correct. §e19 Translucent surfaces§r: normals of water (blue tint) and glass (white tint). §bSplit Screen§r compares a view with the normal image. §bHighlight Broken Pixels§r finds NaN values. §bShadow Map Preview§r shows the shadow map. §bFreeze Noise§r lets you compare settings without flicker
